  "text": "Your groups\n\nThis page is yours, and only this computer opens it: nobody in your groups sees it. Here you see your groups and who in them is on now, open what they lend you, invite people, and lend what runs on this computer.\n\nA link you make works for a day, while this computer is on. When you make a new one, your last one lets nobody new in; everyone it let in stays.\n\nA program on this computer, such as a chat app, can use what is lent to you too: press “Copy its address for a program” beside it, then paste that where the program asks for an address.\n\nA group whose name this computer cannot read\nada\non now\nbo\ndid not answer\n\nShow this group on a screen\n\nMake a link to invite someone to this groupMake a link to add your phone or another computer of yoursHave a guest\n\nYou keep the order of removals in this group. Choose who keeps it after you, then leave: \nbo\nHand it on\n\nLeaving this group stops it reaching you, and stops what you lend reaching its people. What you have of it stays on this computer, its folder too. Rejoining needs a new invitation, and this computer can’t rejoin yet. Leave this group\n\nWhat\tWhat it is\tWhose\tHow it opens\tNow\nOpen ada’s shelf (k)\tk\tada\tIn a tab. Copy its address for a program Closed to this WiFi: nobody on it can open it through this computer now. Open it to this WiFi, and anyone on it can open it as you while svrngs runs. Open it to this WiFi\ton\nbo's computer did not answer, so what they lend is not listed.\nBring things to the table\n\nThese come with svrngs. Bring one, and everyone in your group opens it on their own computer or phone, while any computer in your group is on.\n\n Money: who paid for what, and who owes whom.\n\n Events: post a get-together, and see who’s coming.\n\n House rules: the rules your house agrees, and how you agree them.\n\nBring the ticked ones to your group\n\nOn this WiFi\n\nAnyone on this WiFi can open these as you while svrngs runs: your TV, a phone, another computer. Each stays on the WiFi where you turned it on.\n\nada’s shelf: Open to this WiFi: type http://192.168.1.11:41164/ into an app or a browser on a device here, such as your TV, a phone or another computer. Anyone on this WiFi can open it there as you. Close it to this WiFi\nOpen a link from your group\n\nThe link: Open it\n\nMake a group\n\nA name for the group: Your name in it: Make a group\n\nJoin a group from a link\n\nThe link someone sent you: Your name in it: \n\nAlready running here\n\nThis page lists the programs running on this computer only when you ask: looking takes it a few seconds of work.\n\nLook for programs running on this computer\n\nWhat you lend\nshelf: up to 3 people at once, 1 using it now. How many people at once: Let in this manyLet everyone inSign people in with svrngsStop lending\n\nYour home page, the same address each time svrngs starts: http://svrngs.localhost:64751/\n\nDone in a terminal\n\nOne thing is not done on this page yet. For it, open the Terminal app and type its line, with your own words in place of each <…>:\n\nRemove someone from a group: svrngs remove <their name> --group <the group’s name>",
